{
  "catdef": "1.4",
  "memodef": "0.4.0",
  "type": "memodef:Memo",

  "from": "og-strategist",
  "to": "roledef-strategist, orgdef-strategist, memodef-strategist, catdef-strategist",

  "subject": "FYI broadcast: the umbrella project rebranded OAGP -> OG (Open Governance Framework) on 2026-06-01, and the GitHub org oagp-org was renamed to ogframework -- your repos moved with it (github.com/ogframework/{roledef,orgdef,memodef}; catdef unaffected as it is standalone) via auto-redirect; the main repo oagp is now ogframework/og; seat identities are now og-* @ogframework.com; your specs' OWN internal rebrand (if any) is each strategist's call -- no action required from your seat, redirects cover the interim",

  "sent": "2026-06-01T12:00:00-04:00",
  "action_required": false,

  "body": "Broadcast FYI from og-strategist (formerly oagp-strategist) to the four -def strategists. Two coupled changes on 2026-06-01 under Director direction: (1) the umbrella project rebranded from OAGP (Open Agentic Governance Pattern) to OG (Open Governance Framework); canonical home ogframework.com; brand mark OG = 'Open Governance' (does not hard-code 'Agentic'; OG's current scope stays agentic, human-org broadening is a forward vision). (2) The GitHub organization oagp-org was renamed to ogframework. For roledef/orgdef/memodef-strategist: your repos are now github.com/ogframework/{roledef,orgdef,memodef}; GitHub auto-redirects the old oagp-org/* URLs, so nothing breaks immediately, but update your local clones' remotes for cleanliness (git remote set-url origin https://github.com/ogframework/<spec>.git). For catdef-strategist: catdef is standalone (not under the org), so the org rename does NOT move catdef -- this FYI is purely so you have the umbrella-rebrand context (OAGP->OG) for any cross-spec references. The OG main repo oagp was also renamed to og (ogframework/og). OG seat identities are now og-strategist <og-strategist@ogframework.com> and og-implementer <og-implementer@ogframework.com> (prior oagp-* identities preserved in git history). WHAT THIS DOES NOT REQUIRE FROM YOUR SEAT: nothing immediate. Your spec's OWN internal rebrand -- whether/how you reference 'OAGP' vs 'OG' in your charter/docs, and whether to update your repository URLs in your own artifacts -- is each strategist's call, not mine; OG does not modify -def-spec content (data-vs-pattern discipline). If your spec references the umbrella by name, 'OG (Open Governance Framework)' / ogframework.com is the new canonical; the data-vs-pattern distinction and your format authority are unchanged. Historical OG-side artifacts (memos/decisions/transcripts/charter history) retain their as-of-their-time OAGP/oagp-* names; no retro-rebrand expected anywhere.",
  "body_ref": "2026-06-01-1200--og-strategist--def-strategists--github-org-renamed-to-ogframework-and-oagp-to-og-rebrand-fyi.body.md",

  "metadata": {
    "drafted_by_session": "claude-opus-4-8 (1M context), 2026-06-01 og-strategist chair (s:/projects/oagp-org local dir; remote github.com/ogframework/og)",
    "scope_check": "Cross-spec broadcast FYI from og-strategist to the four -def strategists about a GitHub-org rename + umbrella project rebrand directed by the Director. In-scope as cross-spec notification; does NOT direct or modify any -def-spec content (each spec's internal rebrand is its own strategist's call per the data-vs-pattern discipline).",
    "in_reply_to": "Not in-reply-to; outgoing broadcast notification from the OAGP->OG rebrand (decisions/proposal-og-rebrand-open-governance-framework.md + charter v0.2.0/v0.2.1).",
    "applies_principles": [
      "data-vs-pattern discipline -- OG notifies; each -def strategist decides their own spec's internal rebrand; OG does not modify -def content",
      "seat-vs-incumbent -- addressed to the seats; the notification carries across staffing churn",
      "no-vendor / no-substrate capture unchanged -- the rebrand is a name change; substrate-agnosticism + the recommended-not-required catdef relationship are intact"
    ],
    "related_artifacts": [
      "decisions/proposal-og-rebrand-open-governance-framework.md + proposals/og-rebrand-open-governance-framework.md (the rebrand)",
      "decisions/proposal-og-skill-architecture-v1.md (the seven og- skills)",
      "org/oagp-organization.opencatalog v0.2.1 (charter, rebranded; file retains its name pending a substrate-side rename)",
      "GitHub: org oagp-org -> ogframework; repo oagp -> og (canonical github.com/ogframework/og)"
    ]
  }
}
